    sources: [{ label: "Léon Foucault, 18 September 1819 to 11 February 1868, French physicist at the Paris Observatory: inventor of the Foucault pendulum demonstrating the Earth's rotation in 1851, an early measurement of the speed of light, the discovery of eddy currents, and credited with naming the gyroscope; Copley Medal 1855, Fellow of the Royal Society 1864", href: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A9on_Foucault" }],
