    sources: [ // every label says what the page says and when it was read (12/11/2026, batch 5C)
      { label: "F5 Distributed Cloud Customer Edge; the old address now redirects to F5 Distributed Cloud Services Site, docs-v2, last modified 12 November 2026 (read 2026-11-12): a CE Site is a physical or cloud location where F5 nodes are deployed; a cluster of one or more Linux-based nodes delivered as an ISO or a Kubernetes deployment spec, on a VM, a Kubernetes cluster, commodity hardware or F5 edge hardware; on-a-stick and default-gateway modes; SITE_LOCAL_OUTSIDE and SITE_LOCAL_INSIDE interfaces; call home with a tenant token; 2n+1 control nodes; IPsec/SSL tunnels to the Regional Edges forming an isolated fabric", href: "https://docs.cloud.f5.com/docs/ves-concepts/site" }, // F5 Distributed Cloud Customer Edge; the 
      { label: "F5, F5 Distributed Cloud Customer Edge, concept page, docs-v2, last modified 12 November 2026 (read 2026-11-12): a software-defined execution point extending the F5 SaaS platform into customer environments; full-stack L3 to L7 appliance; Secure Mesh and App Stack flavours; ETCD quorum and the three-node recommendation; single-node only for test; registration with a token; two Regional Edges chosen by GeoIP; certificates rotated; IPsec preferred with SSL fallback; tunnels for management, control and optionally data", href: "https://docs.cloud.f5.com/docs-v2/multi-cloud-network-connect/concepts/f5-xc-customer-edge" }, // F5
      { label: "F5, Customer Edge IP Address and Domain Reference for Firewall or Proxy Settings, published 11 June 2025, last modified 12 November 2026 (read 2026-11-12): mandatory egress IP and domain rules, DNS and NTP; registration and updates to 159.60.141.140 on TCP 443 for Secure Mesh Site v2; RE ranges on TCP 80 and 443 and UDP 4500 and 123, UDP 4500 optional because SSL tunnelling is supported; the single wildcard *.volterra.io or an FQDN list; third-party wildcards removed; Google DNS 8.8.8.8 and 8.8.4.4 and Google NTP unless custom servers are set; port 65500 for local UI and API; IP addresses can change, domains preferred; a plain-text file for automation", href: "https://docs.cloud.f5.com/docs-v2/multi-cloud-network-connect/reference/ce-ip-dom-ref" }, // F5
      { label: "F5, Customer Edge Ecosystem Support (read 2026-11-12): AWS, Azure and GCP with automated cloud sites or Secure Mesh Site v2; OCI, EKS, AKS, GKE and OpenShift Kubernetes Engine, Hyper-V, VMware ESXi 7.0 or later, OpenStack, Nutanix AHV, bare metal and OpenShift Virtualization through Secure Mesh Site v2", href: "https://docs.cloud.f5.com/docs-v2/platform/reference/ce-ecosystem-support" }, // F5
      { label: "F5, Secure Mesh Site v2 FAQs (read 2026-11-12): certified hardware removed; choice of Regional Edges; single registration endpoint; GA and early-access providers; a single node when HA is disabled; HA nodes powered on at least 90 seconds apart with identical resources; no LTE interfaces, no vertical scaling", href: "https://docs.cloud.f5.com/docs-v2/multi-cloud-network-connect/faqs/smsv2-faqs" }, // F5
      { label: "F5, Create Origin Pools (read 2026-11-12): an origin server by IP address on given sites, with the site or virtual site and the inside network, outside network or a segment, and an optional SNAT pool", href: "https://docs.cloud.f5.com/docs-v2/multi-cloud-app-connect/how-to/app-networking/origin-pools" }, // F5
      { label: "F5, F5 Completes Acquisition of Volterra, press release, January 2021 (read 2026-11-12): Volterra described as the first universal edge-as-a-service platform, founded by Ankur Singla and Harshad", href: "https://www.f5.com/company/news/press-releases/f5-completes-acquisition-of-volterra" }, // F5
      { label: "IETF, RFC 4364, BGP/MPLS IP Virtual Private Networks, February 2006 (read 2026-11-12): each VPN site contains one or more Customer Edge (CE) devices attached to Provider Edge (PE) routers; CE devices can be hosts or routers", href: "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4364.txt" }, // IETF
    ], // 8 sources, one object per line
